quick plot

- new patient in the hospital

- therapist called in to calm a hysterical patient

- fear of corners of room

- claims the corners are endless, its living in the corners

- therapist is shaken but unable to calm the patient

- therapist goes home, studies

- finds information of others, one person claims able to see whats in the corners

- thinking it will help, agrees to "see"

- new patient in the hospital. it was me.

Scene 1: quiet halls of a mental hospital. sounds of the hospital, but nothing dramatic -- all expected. Suddenly, hell breaks loose, cacophony of sounds and movement. a new patient has arrived.

Scene 2: padded room. Patient hiding head. We are in the viewpoint of the therapist. We ask a lot of questions. Patient seems obsessed with what is "in between" everything, especially in the corners. There is a deep fear, an obsession beyond measure. We try to force the patient to look at the corners to "shock" him out of the heightened state, but his eyes are bloodshot red when we pull his arms free and his face contorts and he screams at what he sees, thrashing. We must sedate him.

Scene 3: therapist office/home. Cannot sleep, obsessing over the patient and what he saw. never heard of such an obsession, researches to see if anyone has experience with this. finds some websites with creepy texts about occult shit the guy was saying in the hospital. Find a trusted source who did research on the type of claims being made.

Scene 4: Locate the hermit, but hes gone. Weird papers. Weird information. Mechanism needed to unlock his ability to look into the corners.

Scene 5: difficult trip event in the corners, deal with demons on the past, what is his demons? a lack of belief in someone he knew, he was too smart for them, he knew better. Descend into madness. Lose sense of self. Who am I in the corners when its all flipped over? The corners are mirrors, the mirrors are distorted, lost.

Scene 6: awakening in another body. Its a hospital. I hear my voice. It sounds outside of me. Its talking to me about my fears. I don't want to see. I don't want to look. I cry out about the corners, its not my voice, its not my voice, pry my hands away, I am not me, who is that, who is that.

end.

who is he? a know it all. a non-believer. The kind of person firmly set in reality. Considers those who believe in nonsense to be more stupid than imaginable. Disowned his own son because he had become relgious and believed in something more than us existed. prim and proper, his parents never cared for that fantastical shit, and so while it had interested him as a boy, he let those things go for the passions that would gain his fathers praise - science. He thought that the science of the mind would be the best area, so unexplored, but in the end father felt it was just more hogwash. He was likely write, the man felt, and while he continued to do his job, he did it with calousness and carelessness with the leasted cared for people. a mental health hospital, overnight staff in a big city was a place where he could be praised by the affluant, and care little for the suffering.

when he is in an insane place, he has to reflect upon himself in the mirrors. what can he reflect on that will show character growth? he can see himself as his son, he can see himself rejected by his father, he can see his fathers own rejection, he can see how he is god and they are all god and his hurtful approach to himself and the people he cares for has been killing their souls. they cry out to him. his son, his patients, his father who knew he failed. they cry out that he has killed them.

9pm. The hallways echo with madness, but not the stressful kind. The gentle, methodical kind. The slow thumping of a patient's head softly banging against the wall, the raspy emotional moans of another patient. Ambient noises of this kind of place, at this time of night. Ambient noises I had quite learned to enjoy.

I settled in for some evening reading, this time a collection of Psychiatric Art, supposed drawins that showed the innerworkings of the mentally un-wells condition.

Poppy-cock drivel, I assumed and was assured, because insanity is just insanity, plain and simple. All the brains made of meat certainly could not be created without flaw, it is just the nature of randomness. There is no secret message found within the halls of their hole-riddled brain. That was for certain.

The only thing worse was the relgiious! All holes for brains and yet, totally and wholly allows to perform their rituals and damn their bretheren with all their holy and pious talk.